    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d833">

                <pb facs="0832" n="666" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg666"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 711.5914/115</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Minister Egan
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Departmemt of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-08-24T15:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 24, 1916, 3 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>155. Your 323, August 23d, 4 p.m. So far as I know, no such question has been put
                    to the President, and I am certain no official of the Department has made any
                    statement of the kind indicated. So far as I know, there is nothing to indicate
                    that the Senate will not approve the treaty before adjournment.</p>
                <p>You may use this information in your discretion to counteract any impression that
                    the treaty may not be ratified during the present session.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
